## Day 3: IAM 

### IAM (Floci)
- Created IAM user, group, role
- Attached managed policy to group
- Added user to group
- Learned: Users/Groups/Roles/Policies relationship


### Key Concepts
- **IAM User:** Permanent identity for a person
- **IAM Role:** Temporary identity for services or cross-account access
- **Policy:** JSON document defining permissions

##Examples:

aws iam create-user --user-name devops-learner --endpoint-url http://localhost:4566

aws iam create-group --group-name s3-readonly --endpoint-url http://localhost:4566

aws iam attach-group-policy \
  --group-name s3-readonly \
  --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AmazonS3ReadOnlyAccess \
  --endpoint-url http://localhost:4566

aws iam add-user-to-group \
  --user-name devops-learner \
  --group-name s3-readonly \
  --endpoint-url http://localhost:4566


aws iam list-users --endpoint-url http://localhost:4566
aws iam list-groups --endpoint-url http://localhost:4566
aws iam list-attached-group-policies --group-name s3-readonly --endpoint-url http://localhost:4566

aws iam create-role \
  --role-name ec2-role \
  --assume-role-policy-document '{"Version":"2012-10-17","Statement":[{"Effect":"Allow","Principal":{"Service":"ec2.amazonaws.com"},"Action":"sts:AssumeRole"}]}' \
  --endpoint-url http://localhost:4566
